{
 "_notes": "TANK WARS (levels 5-8). Stage models are in group 29: Metal Fox 689, Desert Fox 693, Jungle Fox 691 (the Swamp Fox stage model was not found among the extracted models, it is built procedurally by the view). Scale 2.6 = world units per model unit; offset centres the play field on the origin. Tank body 774 at 0.68 of the stage scale (the real tank is 0.63 model units wide); driver busts 880-894 are in catalog characters[].variants.tank. Offsets are exact: the sim maps game (x, z) to ((x - cx) k, -(z - cz) k), so the stage (level coords) sits at (-cx k, 0, cz k), k = 2.6/1024. Tanks (RAM of levels 5-8): 0784 = treads part5 (anim 0), turrets by weapon 8/9/10/11 = parts 8/9/10/11, mines parts 1-4 (per player), '?' crate part12, drum 18, missile 6, explosions 24+; swamp hover-tank 0774 part0; pilots = character 'tank' variants 0880-0894 (scale 2.6 = stage). EFFECTS (played by realFx from pack 0786's effect scripts, see re/notes/tankWars.md): taFx* are the parts those scripts use (muzzle flashes 6/7/8/15, shell ends 10-13, trails 2/17, lob hops 9/18, bomb throw 0 and blast 1, mine blast 16, crate break 3, wreck 14); taSmoke0-8 = pack 0784 parts 24-32, the 9-frame smoke puff (object 0x1306) where a shell ends on levels 6-8. Bomb pickup/shot: 0786 parts 11-18 (lit-fuse flip-book). Mine flames (L6/L8): 0784 parts 24-32 fire flip-book.",
